@@ -481,8 +481,20 @@ freeze.store.default.allowStoreCreation=true
 # can be set to false to forbid updates of the violations stored for frozen rules
 # default is true
 freeze.store.default.allowStoreUpdate=false
+
+# names new violation files randomly (the default), or deterministically from the rule description
+freeze.store.default.fileNames=description
+
+# integrity handling during initialization: ignore (the default), repair, or fail
+freeze.store.default.integrity=repair
 ----
 
+With `default.fileNames=description`, names are deterministic and safe to use as files in the
+store folder. A fully qualified `RuleViolationFileNameStrategy` implementation can be configured
+instead. `default.integrity=repair` removes broken or resolved entries and repairs safe misplaced
+entries; it requires `default.allowStoreUpdate=true`. `default.integrity=fail` reports integrity
+problems without changing the store.
+
 This can help in CI environments to prevent misconfiguration:
 For example, a CI build should probably never create a new the violation store, but operate on
 an existing one.
